WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.236 --> 00:00:03.737
Izzie saw Ethan in the hallway ahead of her.

2
00:00:03.777 --> 00:00:07.079
She thought he was nicer than the other boys.

3
00:00:07.819 --> 00:00:15.663
She hoped they could be partners at Kids Central Camp one day.

4
00:00:30.356 --> 00:00:31.617
In the gym Mr.

5
00:00:31.657 --> 00:00:32.999
Dunn was sitting at a table.

6
00:00:33.019 --> 00:00:36.522
"What's the string for?"

7
00:00:36.902 --> 00:00:37.603
Ethan asked.

8
00:00:37.623 --> 00:00:42.167
"Today we're making friendship bracelets," Mr.

9
00:00:42.207 --> 00:00:42.847
Dunn said.

10
00:00:42.867 --> 00:00:46.270
"Friendship bracelets," Izzie thought.

11
00:00:46.290 --> 00:00:52.536
"I could make one for—" "Bracelets are for girls!"

12
00:00:53.036 --> 00:00:53.717
said Bobby.

13
00:00:53.737 --> 00:00:57.000
"No, they're not," Ethan said.

14
00:00:57.764 --> 00:01:00.205
"At my school in California everyone wore them."

15
00:01:00.225 --> 00:01:05.867
"Well, my sister and her friends wear friendship bracelets," Bobby said.

16
00:01:05.887 --> 00:01:08.128
"I think they're goofy."

17
00:01:09.469 --> 00:01:11.710
"They are not goofy," Mr.

18
00:01:11.750 --> 00:01:12.410
Dunn said.

19
00:01:12.430 --> 00:01:15.471
"They're part of a meaningful tradition."

20
00:01:16.532 --> 00:01:17.552
He looked at Bobby.

21
00:01:17.572 --> 00:01:22.274
"When a friend gives you a bracelet, you should never cut it off.

22
00:01:23.355 --> 00:01:26.616
You wear it for as long as the two of you remain friends."

23
00:01:28.360 --> 00:01:30.021
"I can't wait to make mine!"

24
00:01:30.502 --> 00:01:31.222
said Izzie.

25
00:01:31.242 --> 00:01:34.945
"First choose three colors," Mr.

26
00:01:35.005 --> 00:01:35.886
Dunn instructed.

27
00:01:35.906 --> 00:01:38.147
"This is pretty."

28
00:01:39.128 --> 00:01:41.310
Izzie reached for a bundle of blue thread.

29
00:01:42.070 --> 00:01:45.433
But her hand bumped into another hand reaching for the same one.

30
00:01:45.453 --> 00:01:48.495
"Sorry," Ethan mumbled.

31
00:01:48.515 --> 00:01:50.477
"I'll pick a different one."

32
00:01:50.497 --> 00:01:53.739
"You can choose the same color," Mr.

33
00:01:53.779 --> 00:01:54.420
Dunn said.

34
00:01:55.372 --> 00:02:00.013
"Izzie, measure out sixty centimeters, and then give Ethan the thread."

35
00:02:02.594 --> 00:02:05.475
Everyone measured and cut six strands of thread.

36
00:02:10.336 --> 00:02:10.916
Then Mr.

37
00:02:10.956 --> 00:02:12.317
Dunn showed them what to do.

38
00:02:12.337 --> 00:02:16.318
"Now tie a knot ten centimeters from one end.

39
00:02:17.478 --> 00:02:19.559
Next tape that end to the table.

40
00:02:20.639 --> 00:02:23.600
After that separate the strands by color.

41
00:02:24.640 --> 00:02:26.841
There should be two strands of each color."

42
00:02:26.861 --> 00:02:29.903
"Now we're ready to weave!"

43
00:02:30.343 --> 00:02:31.024
said Nina.

44
00:02:31.964 --> 00:02:33.085
Mr. Dunn nodded.

45
00:02:34.125 --> 00:02:36.847
"Start with the strand all the way to the left.

46
00:02:38.007 --> 00:02:40.589
Use it to tie a knot around the string next to it.

47
00:02:41.930 --> 00:02:43.891
Keep going all the way across.

48
00:02:45.912 --> 00:02:49.273
Once you've knotted each string, start again on the left.

49
00:02:52.735 --> 00:02:53.576
Do you understand?"

50
00:02:53.928 --> 00:02:55.109
Mr. Dunn asked.

51
00:02:55.129 --> 00:02:57.731
"Yep!" Izzie said.

52
00:02:58.692 --> 00:03:00.394
This looked like it would take a while.

53
00:03:01.495 --> 00:03:03.136
She wanted to finish hers today.

54
00:03:03.156 --> 00:03:05.438
"Weave away!

55
00:03:06.439 --> 00:03:08.681
Ask me if you need help," said Mr.

56
00:03:08.761 --> 00:03:16.407
Dunn. making mine for you," Nina whispered to Izzie.

57
00:03:18.069 --> 00:03:19.990
Izzie looked at her friend and swallowed.

58
00:03:20.010 --> 00:03:23.833
"Thanks." Then she got back to work.

59
00:03:24.933 --> 00:03:26.254
Knot, knot, knot.

60
00:03:27.314 --> 00:03:28.334
Knot, knot, knot.

61
00:03:29.475 --> 00:03:30.175
Start again.

62
00:03:32.836 --> 00:03:34.097
Finally she was done.

63
00:03:36.638 --> 00:03:39.739
Izzie's hands were cramping and her neck hurt from bending over.

64
00:03:41.140 --> 00:03:42.680
But her bracelet looked great.

65
00:03:43.761 --> 00:03:44.741
"Okay, campers.

66
00:03:46.102 --> 00:03:50.304
Time to get out into that sunshine and play some kickball," Mr.

67
00:03:50.364 --> 00:03:51.004
Dunn said.

68
00:03:52.424 --> 00:03:56.206
"If you're not done with your bracelets, you can finish them at home," Mr.

69
00:03:56.226 --> 00:03:56.847
Dunn added.

70
00:03:58.167 --> 00:04:00.549
He leaned over and looked at Izzie's bracelet.

71
00:04:00.569 --> 00:04:03.590
"Nice job, Izzie," he said.

72
00:04:03.610 --> 00:04:05.771
"You worked hard today."

73
00:04:05.791 --> 00:04:08.453
"Thanks," said Izzie.

74
00:04:09.453 --> 00:04:11.014
She was glad she was finished.

75
00:04:13.476 --> 00:04:17.218
When everything was put away, the kids lined up to go outside.

76
00:04:18.518 --> 00:04:20.960
Izzie was behind Ethan at the end of the line.

77
00:04:21.936 --> 00:04:25.537
She saw Ethan stuff his unfinished bracelet in his pocket.

78
00:04:25.557 --> 00:04:27.818
"Hey, Ethan."

79
00:04:28.078 --> 00:04:29.238
Izzie poked his arm.

80
00:04:29.258 --> 00:04:31.699
"I made my bracelet for you.

81
00:04:32.899 --> 00:04:33.699
Will you wear it?"

82
00:04:34.179 --> 00:04:34.840
she mumbled.

83
00:04:34.860 --> 00:04:39.881
"Sure. Thanks, that's really nice," he told Izzie.

84
00:04:39.901 --> 00:04:48.163
"Cool." Grinning, Izzie tied the bracelet on his wrist.

85
00:04:49.504 --> 00:04:50.984
Then she ran to the blacktop.
